From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: back off the SigDet/CDR recovery

an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround() runs from every USXGMII pcs_get_state(),
which phylink calls once per second. Whenever the PCS reports link down
while the RX SigDet module still sees a signal, it resets the CDR and
reports link down for that poll.

That is also the state a freshly renegotiated link goes through: the
partner restarts in-band AN, and the PCS needs more than one poll round
to regain block lock. Resetting the CDR on every poll restarts the lock
acquisition the AN depends on, which stretches a short renegotiation
window into a repeating reset loop.

Only consider the recovery once the CDR had time to lock, and back off
exponentially between retries. A PCS that is down while in-band AN has
not completed is expected to be transient, so keep a small grace of poll
rounds before resetting it; a PCS that stays stuck since bringup is
still recovered after that grace.

Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2024 AIROHA Inc
  * Author: Christian Marangi <ansuelsmth@gmail.com>
  */
+#include <linux/jiffies.h>
 #include <linux/math.h>
 #include <linux/phy/phy.h>
 #include <linux/pcs/pcs-airoha.h>
@@ -3579,25 +3580,59 @@
 	return count >= AIROHA_PCS_MAX_RX_SIGDET_PRESENCE_CNT;
 }
 
+/* In-band AN poll rounds a PCS that is stuck since bringup may stay down
+ * before the CDR recovery is still allowed to kick in.
+ */
+#define AIROHA_PCS_RXLOCK_AN_GRACE	3
+
 int an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv, int index)
 {
 	struct airoha_pcs_maps *maps = &priv->maps[index];
-	u32 val = 0;
+	u32 an_done = 0, val = 0;
 
 	/* Check if PCS is UP or Down */
 	regmap_read(maps->usxgmii_pcs, AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_STUS_1, &val);
-	if (val & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_RX_LINK_STATUS_UP)
+	if (val & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_RX_LINK_STATUS_UP) {
+		priv->rxlock_an_polls[index] = 0;
+		priv->rxlock_backoff[index] = 0;
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	/* Validate if this is consistent with RX SigDet module */
 	if (!an7581_pcs_have_rx_signal(priv, index))
 		return 0;
 
+	/* A PCS that reports link down while in-band AN is still running is
+	 * expected: the partner restarts AN after every copper renegotiation,
+	 * and resetting the CDR here would abort the lock acquisition the AN
+	 * depends on. Keep the recovery for a PCS that stays stuck, so a
+	 * bringup failure is still handled.
+	 */
+	regmap_read(maps->usxgmii_pcs, AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_AN_STATS_2,
+		    &an_done);
+	if (!(an_done & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_AN_COMPLETE) &&
+	    priv->rxlock_an_polls[index]++ < AIROHA_PCS_RXLOCK_AN_GRACE)
+		return 0;
+	priv->rxlock_an_polls[index] = 0;
+
+	/* Give the CDR time to lock after a reset before resetting it again. */
+	if (time_before(jiffies, priv->rxlock_next[index]))
+		return 0;
+
 	/* If PCS is down but RX SigDet module detected signal,
 	 * trigger CDR reset.
 	 */
 	an7581_pcs_cdr_reset(priv, index, PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_NA, false);
 
+	/* Back off exponentially (1, 2, 4, then 8 seconds) so a PCS that
+	 * needs longer to regain block lock is not reset on every poll.
+	 */
+	priv->rxlock_next[index] = jiffies +
+		HZ * (1UL << (priv->rxlock_backoff[index] > 3 ?
+			      3 : priv->rxlock_backoff[index]));
+	if (priv->rxlock_backoff[index] < 3)
+		priv->rxlock_backoff[index]++;
+
 	/* Report there is an error with Link Detection and we
 	 * should test again later.
 	 */
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h
@@ -1674,6 +1677,11 @@
 	u8 pon_tx_term_sel;
 	u8 pon_rx_term_sel;
 
+	/* SigDet/CDR recovery bookkeeping, one slot per PCS instance. */
+	unsigned long rxlock_next[2];
+	u8 rxlock_an_polls[2];
+	u8 rxlock_backoff[2];
+
 	/* pcs-an7581.c updates the PON PMA stage and calibration state. */
 	u32 pon_stage;
 	s32 pon_last_error;
